{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789218672,"nonce":"MGoNlyboCd0rOgSBRyVnvCtoQeg=","title":"Automatic drop costs one branch per node over hand-written release","message":"Measured 1.04x Cranelift, 1.06x LLVM on binary trees against a\nhand-written release, at identical peak RSS. Counted rather than timed:\nthe glue has 2 branches and 2 loads per node, the hand-written release\n1 branch and 3 loads. The hand-written one tests self.left != null once\nand releases both children inside; the glue tests each field\nindependently because the type does not promise the children are null\ntogether. Inherent unless the type can say \"these fields are absent\ntogether\" or a shape analysis proves it. Moving synthesis ahead of the\noptimisation sweep was tried and measured no change; reverted.","files":null}]}